"""Content of the "CSM RA" tab: the risk management process map of Regulation (EU) 402/2013 and the guided
assessment that walks a proposer through it. Built into the map by navigator.build_nav().

Sources (all in the library): Regulation (EU) 402/2013 as amended by (EU) 2015/1136 (consolidated 3.8.2015) –
Articles 2–18, Annex I and its Appendix figure, Annexes II and III; ERA's guide for the application of the CSM,
the collection of examples, the guide on harmonised design targets, the explanatory note on the CSM assessment
body, AsBo RFUs 01–04, 08, 11, clarification notes ERA1209/063, /146, /186, /039; Regulation (EU) 2018/545
Art. 13; Regulation (EU) 2018/762; Regulation (EU) 1078/2012.

The Regulation still cites Directives 2004/49/EC and 2008/57/EC; the text here names the provisions that
replaced them in Directives (EU) 2016/798 and 2016/797.

Each node:  id, t (title), kind, x/y/w/h (box centre and size), sub (bullet lines for 'stage' boxes),
  law   what the Regulation requires (paragraphs, with article / point numbers)
  era   what ERA guidance and the AsBo RFUs add
  prac  practice notes – NOT binding, shown separately and marked as such
  ev    evidence the step normally leaves behind
  cen   how the step maps onto EN 50126 / EN 50129
  r     {role: one paragraph} – shown when that role lens is on; a node without text for a role is dimmed
  refs  resolved like task-path refs (family key, short name, cited label or file-name fragment)
  va    [(mode, id)] boxes of the Vehicle authorisation tab to cross-link
Edges: (from, to, label, style, route) – style "", "dash", "yes" or "no"; route None (automatic), "lane"
(straight across to a lane box), "elbow" (down, then across) or a number (x of the vertical run of a loop).
"""

